meta {
  name: Get Bug Report
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/bug-reports/{{bugReportId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("carries the full description and the captured context", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.description).to.contain("Motivation Hub");
    expect(body.context.route).to.equal("/dashboard/producer");
    expect(body.context.viewport.width).to.equal(1512);
    expect(body.context.theme).to.equal("dark");
  });

  test("screenshots come back signed, with no storage key", function () {
    const shot = res.getBody().screenshots[0];
    expect(shot).to.have.property("id");
    expect(shot).to.have.property("url");
    expect(shot).to.not.have.property("key");
    expect(res.getBody().screenshotUrlExpiresIn).to.be.a("number");
  });

  test("size is what storage reported, not what the client declared", function () {
    // `Create Bug Report` declared 20480; the upload was a short text stand-in.
    expect(res.getBody().screenshots[0].size).to.not.equal(20480);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /platform/bug-reports/:id — one report in full

  Everything the detail sheet renders: the description, the captured browser
  context, the screenshots, and the triage state.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:bugs:read`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ## Screenshots are signed here, and expire

  Each screenshot comes back with a short-lived **inline** presigned GET — so
  the page renders it straight into an `<img>` and clicking opens it in the
  browser's own viewer. The storage key never crosses the wire in either
  direction; the client identifies a screenshot by its subdocument `id`.

  `screenshotUrlExpiresIn` (300s by default, from
  `STORAGE_DOWNLOAD_URL_TTL_SECONDS`) is echoed so the client can keep its cache
  staleness under it — `BugReportDetailSheet` pins `staleTime` to 120s for
  exactly this reason. A sheet reopened after the TTL re-signs rather than
  rendering broken images.

  `contentType` is overridden on the signed URL: an image stored as
  `application/octet-stream` downloads instead of rendering, whatever the
  disposition says.

  ## The size assertion above

  `size` is read from `HeadObject` at create time, not from the request body —
  which is why it does not match the `20480` the presign and create bodies
  declared. That is the whole point: a presigned PUT signs only the content
  type, so a declared size is a claim about a file the API has never seen.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "id": "68f3…c21",
    "status": "new",
    "severity": "high",
    "description": "The leaderboard still shows…",
    "reporterName": "Casey Rivera",
    "reporterEmail": "producer@demoagency.local",
    "agencyId": "68a1…f09",
    "agencyName": "Demo Agency",
    "context": {
      "url": "http://localhost:5173/dashboard/producer?range=month",
      "route": "/dashboard/producer",
      "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0 …",
      "viewport": { "width": 1512, "height": 916 },
      "theme": "dark"
    },
    "screenshots": [{
      "id": "68f3…c22",
      "filename": "leaderboard-stale.png",
      "contentType": "image/png",
      "size": 33,
      "url": "http://localhost:9000/sfa-uploads/…&response-content-disposition=inline…"
    }],
    "screenshotUrlExpiresIn": 300,
    "screenshotCount": 1,
    "internalNotes": null,
    "statusUpdatedAt": null,
    "statusUpdatedByName": null,
    "createdAt": "2026-09-01T14:22:07.113Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-01T14:22:07.113Z"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `platform:bugs:read`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such report, **and** any malformed id: an invalid
    ObjectId is a 404 rather than a 400, so probing tells an attacker nothing.
}
